  "title": "Central African Republic Gold Mine Collapse: 100+ Dead Amid Landslide",
  "summary": "A significant goldmine collapse in Central African Republic (CAR) led to over 100 deaths, with local officials noting the risk of further casualties as recovery efforts continue. The incident occurred in a remote village near the border with Cameroon, and footage showed an avalanche of sand, likely caused by a landslide.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "More than 100 people have died after an artisanal goldmine collapse in western Central African Republic (CAR) due to a landslide.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Local officials and aid workers reported the death toll is likely to rise as recovery efforts continue.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The landslide happened on Tuesday afternoon in the village of Zamboye, about 50km from Baboua and close to the border of Cameroon.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
